  "2026-10-06T11:38:31.267Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict live all-status corpus returned 2897 of 2897 with complete reads and zero omissions or unreadable rows. Exact run and issue-number searches found no existing owner. Exact fixture-path matches identify shipped pm-2x67z9 and pm-gh1393 whose complete live metadata and verified histories were read. The generic platform-recurrence measurement issue does not own these specific fixture repairs. Open and in-progress inventories were refreshed."
  "2026-10-06T11:46:34.014Z","harness:codex","Red evidence: scheduled run 37454181508 at 6436916 has real macOS approved-byte verifier failure and both Windows schema-policy cases rejected by the Node ESM loader. Full affected fixtures and workflows were read before editing. The bounded repair uses a canonical file URL and actual Node SHA-256 comparison before chmod while keeping the same immutable digest and both corrupt-byte and genuine history-drift refusals. Nightly explicitly provisions the existing pinned Bun 1.4.0 for new packed dual-runtime acceptance. The completed SDK source coverage remains byte-unchanged."
  "2026-10-06T11:55:27.755Z","harness:codex","Local platform tranche passes all 21 linked cases, including actual approved/corrupt SHA-256 verification before chmod and real source/global history drift refusal. Fresh official Codecov v11.3.1 release metadata still publishes the exact pinned digest and 10402464-byte asset; no pin or security condition changed. Latest pm-changelog 2026.10.5 generates and checks the three completed delivery records. The full-source 9789-case coverage receipt remains unchanged by the subsequent workflow and fixture-only portability fixes. Fresh branch-head nightly macOS and Windows proof is still required before this issue closes."
